   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch3/q2",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Use the standard results for summations to show that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}(5r-2)^2=\\frac{1}{6}n(an^2+bn+c)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{k}(5r-2)^2=94k^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
