   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^2\"></span> to show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}(3r^2+8r+3)=\\frac{1}{2}n(2n+5)(n+3)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{12}\\left(3r^2+8r+3+k(2^{r-1})\\right)=3520\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>find the exact value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
