   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Prove by induction that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^2=\\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(2n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\"></span> to show that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r(r+6)(r-6)=\\frac{1}{4}n(n+1)(n-8)(n+9)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> that satisfies<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r(r+6)(r-6)=17\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
